orow(38, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'OUR FATHERS CAME INTO THE LAND AND BLESSING CAME AT THEIR FEET: "HOUSES FULL OF ALL GOOD WHICH YOU DID NOT FILL, HEWN CISTERNS WHICH YOU DID NOT HEW" (6:11) — R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: IS IT NOT KNOWN YOU DID NOT FILL THEM, YOU HAVE ONLY NOW COME? … "VINEYARDS AND OLIVES WHICH YOU DID NOT PLANT" — WHAT THEN DO "FILL", "HEW", "PLANT" TEACH? YOUR MERIT CAUSED IT; FORTY YEARS THE LAND\'S DWELLERS BUILT AND DUG AND PLANTED FOR ISRAEL\'S COMING; "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" — ISRAEL EATS AND IS SATISFIED WHILE THEY STINTED THEIR OWN WIVES AND SONS. The row on 11:10 (the piska\'s head; the Egypt-and-Canaan contrast) citing 6:11 THREE TIMES in the Hebrew ({SP_(38, 10, "באת", "ברכה", "לרגלם")} "blessing came at their feet"): 6:11\'s three "which you did not" read as REDUNDANT (obviously not — you had just come) and therefore as MERIT — the land prepared by others for forty years; the ink: "houses full of all good" one seat, "hewn cisterns" one, "vineyards and olive trees" 6:11, Joshua 24:13 and Nehemiah 9:25 — the list\'s two retellings (computed); "and you shall eat and be satisfied" 6:11, 8:10, 11:15 (computed). The middah: a clause read as idle and given a teaching (E10 — the repetition signifies); the "forty years" the tape\'s own count. Fresh in both files.')
orow(41, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH I COMMAND YOU THIS DAY" (11:13) — ONE WHO HEARS A WORD FROM THE LEAST IN ISRAEL, LET IT BE AS FROM A SAGE, FROM THE SAGES, FROM THE SANHEDRIN ("MASTERS OF ASSEMBLIES", ECCLESIASTES 12:11), FROM MOSES, FROM THE MIGHTY ONE — "GIVEN FROM ONE SHEPHERD", "SHEPHERD OF ISRAEL, GIVE EAR" (PSALM 80:2), "HEAR, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4). The row on 11:13 ({SP_(41, 14, "כשומע", "מפי", "הגבורה")} "as one hearing from the mouth of the Mighty One"): 6:4 quoted as the LAST proof of the ladder — the creed itself the Mighty One\'s own word heard; the row cites 6:4 in both files; nothing on the chapter\'s law. Fresh.')
orow(41, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHY "WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" (11:13) WHEN "WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" (6:5) IS ALREADY SAID? THERE THE INDIVIDUAL, HERE THE COMMUNITY; THERE STUDY, HERE THE DEED — YOU HEARD, DO; YOU DID YOURS, I DO MINE: "AND I WILL GIVE THE RAIN" (11:14). The row on 11:13 ({SP_(41, 20, "להלן", "ליחיד", "כאן", "לצבור")} "there to the individual, here to the community"): THE NUMBER OF THE SUFFIX made the reading — 6:5\'s SINGULAR "your heart" the individual\'s study, 11:13\'s PLURAL the community\'s deed (the English\'s notes: the suffixes); THE INK AGREES: "with all your heart and with all your soul" SINGULAR seven seats, all Deuteronomy\'s (4:29, 6:5, 10:12, 26:16, 30:2, 6, 10), PLURAL four (11:13, 13:4, Joshua 22:5, 23:14) — computed; the chapter\'s register singular-only at fifteen verses (the design). The middah: two seats of one phrase distinguished by their grammatical number (E10 — repetition signifies, the distinction the number). Fresh in both files.')
orow(104, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU SHALL NOT BOIL A KID IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK" (14:21) — WHY SAID THREE TIMES? AGAINST THE THREE COVENANTS THE HOLY ONE CUT WITH ISRAEL: AT HOREB, IN THE PLAINS OF MOAB, AT MOUNT GERIZIM AND EBAL. The row on 14:21 ({SP_(104, 8, "אחת", "בחורב")} "one at Horeb"): THE ENGLISH EXPORT ALONE writes "(Dt.6:1ff.)" beside "at Horeb" — the translator\'s own parenthesis (his note calls the whole row an interpolation from the Mekhilta Kaspa 20); the Hebrew names no verse — a citation form new to the scan (the design\'s lesson), read and excluded from the chapter\'s claims. Fresh.')
orow(201, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL UTTERLY DESTROY THEM" (20:17) — MIGHT THEIR SPOIL BE FORBIDDEN TO YOU? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND HOUSES FULL OF ALL GOOD" (6:11). The row on 20:15-17 (the seven nations\' ban; {SP_(201, 3, "יכול", "תהא", "בזתם", "אסורה", "לך")} "might their spoil be forbidden to you"): 6:11 read as a LAW — the ban on the seven nations falls on the people, not the property; the houses "full of all good" are the promise\'s content and so permitted — a CALL from the war-law\'s cell into this chapter\'s verse (the compile at 4b: the cherem runner\'s edge; Deuteronomy 20 not yet read). The ink: "houses full of all good" one seat (computed). The middah: a later law bounded by an earlier promise (I13\'s form — the two verses reconciled; the Sifrei\'s own, LR1). Fresh in both files.')
orow(258, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD WALKS IN THE MIDST OF YOUR CAMP" (23:15) — FROM HERE THEY SAID: A MAN SHALL NOT RECITE THE SHEMA BESIDE THE LAUNDERERS\' VAT, NOR ENTER A BATH-HOUSE OR A TANNERY WITH SCROLLS AND TEFILLIN IN HIS HAND. The head row of piska 258 ({SP_(258, 1, "לא", "יקרא", "אדם", "את", "שמע")} "a man shall not recite the Shema"): the Shema NAMED AS A TEXT by its first word — the camp\'s cleanness (23:13-15) the ground for where it may not be said; Mishnah Berakhot 3:5 the case row (the English\'s note; the docket\'s — "the recitation" cell). The English cites "(Dt.6:4 ff.)" for the name; the Hebrew\'s שמע ("Hear") bare — the scan\'s union found it. The middah: a place-rule derived from the camp\'s holiness (I12\'s kin — the meaning from the passage). Fresh in both files.')
orow(306, 37, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN I CALL THE NAME OF THE LORD, ASCRIBE GREATNESS" (32:3) — R. YOSE: WHENCE THE RESPONSE TO "BLESS THE LORD" IN THE SYNAGOGUE; THE THREE FOR THE GRACE; "AMEN" AFTER A BLESSING; AND WHENCE THAT THE MINISTERING ANGELS DO NOT MENTION HIS NAME ABOVE UNTIL ISRAEL MENTION IT BELOW — "HEAR, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4), THEN "WHEN THE MORNING STARS SANG TOGETHER" (JOB 38:7). The Song\'s row ({SP_(306, 37, "שאין", "מלאכי", "השרת", "מזכירים", "שמו")} "that the ministering angels do not mention His name"): 6:4 the earth\'s naming that precedes heaven\'s — the liturgy\'s order; the English\'s form the response line "blessed be the name …" after the Shema (31:6\'s interjection). Nothing on the chapter\'s law. Fresh.')
orow(355, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'"THERE IS NONE LIKE GOD, O JESHURUN" (33:26) — ISRAEL SAYS "THERE IS NONE LIKE GOD" AND THE HOLY SPIRIT SAYS "JESHURUN"; ISRAEL "WHO IS LIKE YOU AMONG THE GODS" (EXODUS 15:11) — "HAPPY ARE YOU, ISRAEL, WHO IS LIKE YOU" (33:29); ISRAEL "HEAR, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4) — THE HOLY SPIRIT "WHO IS LIKE YOUR PEOPLE ISRAEL, ONE NATION IN THE EARTH" (1 CHRONICLES 17:21); THE APPLE AND THE LILY (SONG 2:3, 2:2); "THIS IS MY GOD" (EXODUS 15:2) — "THIS PEOPLE I FORMED" (ISAIAH 43:21); PSALM 89:18 — ISAIAH 49:3. The row on 33:26 (the piska\'s head 33:20; {SP_(355, 27, "ומי", "כעמך", "ישראל", "גוי", "אחד")} "and who is like Your people Israel, one nation"): THE CREED ANSWERED — Israel\'s "the LORD is ONE" met by heaven\'s "ONE nation"; the word אחד ("one") the hinge of the pair; THE HEBREW CITES IT AS "IBID." — "(שם ו ד)" ("there, 6:4") after the 33:29 citation — the form the book-name scan misses (the design\'s lesson; the English\'s "(Dt.6:4)" caught it). The ink: "one nation" at {P("גוי", "אחד")} (computed — the Chronicles seat and its Samuel twin). The middah: E27 (symmetry — the six antiphonal pairs); the Mekhilta Shirah 3 the parallel (the English\'s note). Fresh in both files.')

